---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout title="Patch v0.107.1">
  <div class="page-header">
    <h1>v0.107.1 Main-Branch Update</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">Changes from v0.107.0 &rarr; v0.107.1 &mdash; derived from decompiled game data</p>
  </div>

  <div style="max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto;">

    <p class="desc-text">
      v0.107.1 is Mega Crit's second major <strong>main-branch</strong> release &mdash; "4 patches in 1" that
      promotes the entire beta line to the default branch. Because this wiki already tracked the beta builds
      (<a href={`${base}patches/v0-105-1/`}>v0.105.1</a> and
      <a href={`${base}patches/v0-107-0/`}>v0.107.0</a>), almost all of the content and balance changes in the
      official notes &mdash; the new <a href={`${base}monsters/aeonglass/`}>Aeonglass</a> Act 3 boss replacing
      Doormaker, the reworked <a href={`${base}monsters/infested-prism/`}>Infested Prism</a>, the
      <a href={`${base}cards/scare/`}>Scare</a> rework, and dozens of card tweaks &mdash; were already present
      in the wiki's data. A field-by-field diff of the decompiled game data between v0.107.0 and v0.107.1 shows
      <strong>no balance or content changes</strong>: identical cards, monsters, relics, potions, powers,
      events, and encounters.
    </p>

    <p class="desc-text">
      The one change that genuinely affects gameplay for <em>everyone</em> &mdash; and the headline item in the
      data &mdash; is the <strong>RNG rework</strong>. Two features that are new to all players this patch
      (<strong>Steam Workshop</strong> support and the <strong>Bestiary</strong>) are engine/UI features with no
      representation in the entity data this wiki extracts.
    </p>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════ -->
    <!-- RNG REWORK                      -->
    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════ -->
    <h2 class="section-heading" id="rng" style="margin-top: 2rem;">RNG Rework</h2>

    <p class="desc-text">
      Each run drives several independent pseudo-random number generators (deck draw, combat rewards, event
      choices, etc.), each seeded from the run seed. The old seeding strategy left those generators
      <strong>correlated</strong>: knowing one outcome (e.g. your first act) let you predict an unrelated one
      (e.g. the curse from Neow's Bones), halving the effective pool. v0.107.1 replaces the PRNG with the modern
      <strong>xoshiro256**</strong> algorithm, producing evenly distributed, human-undetectable results.
    </p>

    <p class="desc-text">
      In the decompiled source this shows up as RNG construction being centralised: per-relic seed arithmetic
      like <code>new Rng((uint)(RunState.Rng.Seed + NetId + GetDeterministicHashCode("FurCoat")))</code> is
      replaced by <code>new Rng(base.Owner, base.Id)</code>. It changes which outcomes a given seed produces, but
      not any card, relic, or enemy stats. The beta-fix notes also call out fewer cases of daily runs diverging
      based on a player's network ID.
    </p>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════ -->
    <!-- NEW FEATURES                    -->
    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════ -->
    <h2 class="section-heading" id="features" style="margin-top: 2rem;">New Features (not data-visible)</h2>

    <table class="stat-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Steam Workshop</strong></td>
          <td>Official Workshop support &mdash; browse and install mods directly, auto-synced across devices. The integrated mod loader has existed since launch; this exposes it.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>The Bestiary</strong></td>
          <td>New Compendium screen listing encountered monsters with their moves and animations. More stats and lore planned.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════ -->
    <!-- ALREADY DOCUMENTED              -->
    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════ -->
    <h2 class="section-heading" id="already-documented" style="margin-top: 2rem;">Already in the Wiki</h2>

    <p class="desc-text">
      The official v0.107.1 notes are a consolidation of the beta patches. The balance and content changes they
      list were extracted into this wiki as they landed during the beta. See the corresponding patch pages for
      the data-level detail:
    </p>

    <ul class="desc-text">
      <li>
        <a href={`${base}patches/v0-107-0/`}>v0.107.0</a> &mdash; Scare replaces Follow Through, Predator to
        Common, Shatter and Astral Pulse reworks, Ebb removed / Tainted added, Infested Prism nerf, and many
        card stat changes.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={`${base}patches/v0-105-1/`}>v0.105.1</a> &mdash; Doormaker boss replaced by Aeonglass,
        Conflagration and Drum of Battle reworks, Regent block nerfs, three new Ancient (Neow) relics, Axebot
        encounter reduced to a single bot.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="desc-text" style="font-size: 0.85rem; margin-top: 1rem;">
      Beyond the RNG rework, v0.107.1's own contribution over v0.107.0 is non-data: bug fixes, crash fixes,
      multiplayer state-divergence fixes, controller-navigation polish, new art/audio, and additional
      translations. None of these alter the extracted entity stats, so they are not itemised here.
    </p>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>
